## DAT toolchain rationalization policy

- Every repository tool must have one explicit responsibility. Tool presence is not justification for continued use.
- Prefer one authoritative tool per responsibility unless distinct layers require distinct tools.
- Confirm usage and call paths before removing a dependency, runtime manager, test runner, CLI, or configuration.
- A tool that is bundled with another tool but is not part of the DAT workflow is not automatically a removal candidate; it must simply not become a competing workflow.
- Current authoritative package manager: pnpm `10.24.0`.
- npm/npx are bundled with Node but are not authoritative DAT package-management workflows.
- Vitest owns unit/integration testing; Playwright owns real-browser/E2E testing. They are complementary, not duplicates.
